From da0ec2805910ca8eea097d61c6258321ab3103d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:27:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/24] Open read-only when a writable open is refused because
 the data file cannot sync

Where the data file cannot sync (#2242), an open that would convert,
migrate, promote or repair the file (and so shrink its log) was refused
and the database could not be opened at all. The refusal is now marked,
and LiteEngine reopens with ReadOnly (and the legacy index scan, which
needs no migration): reads work, every write throws an IOException that
names the cause and leaves the engine readable, and $database reports
readOnlyReason without a write.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UFnsmor6qyZMSd1VoKwfJh
